{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1505418-is-it-feasible-to-homebrew-a-5th-agenda-that-is-conceptually-distinct","id":1505418,"title":"Is it feasible to homebrew a 5th Agenda that is conceptually distinct?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-15T02:04:39-07:00","id":1505418,"title":"Is it feasible to homebrew a 5th Agenda that is conceptually distinct?","content":"This is all I really managed to write in this regard, but it doesn't really feel meaningfully different from a specific combination of Integrator + Tempter. Is this concept for a 5th Agenda worth expanding, and if yes, how could it be done?<br /> <br /> <u><b>ASSIMILATORS</b></u><br /> \ufeff<br /> <i>&quot;I am better than God, and it is my divine birthright to inherit his cosmos that he left unfinished. I will evolve and metamorphose into my own deity, and I will exorcise and reincarnate the scripture-algorithms and machine-temples of God! My new pantheon of servitors-saints and automaton-avatars will assimilate the Shadow, the Underworld, the Hedge, the Astral, and every Facility between Heaven and Earth if need be to overthrow God and remake his Heaven into my Hell!&quot;</i><br /> \ufeff<br /> The Assimilators are Demons who want to become like unto God in the sense of turning communities and institutions into creeds and temples with the end goal of replicating the mechanisms and miracles of the God-Machine. They favor Cults which include other Major Templates, such as Werewolves and their adjunct talents in order to cultivate and engineer modifications and upgrades for the Shadow and its Spirits. This in turn establishes a paradigm where the spiritual ecosystem treats the Demon as its programmer and administrator.<br /> \ufeff<br /> Assimilatord specialize in applying a combination of the Expanded Hijacking System (see below) + Cults + News Maps Of Hell from the ST's Guide. To do this, these Demons use ideological and metaphysical methodologies and techniques for subverting and appropriating the Cultists, Cryptids and Angels of the God-Machine. For example: should they assimilate Werewolves and their adjunct talents, they focus on targeting Infrastructures which impede Sacred Hunts and damage the spiritual ecosystem with undesired types of Resonances.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>Expanded Infrastructure Hijacking</b></u><br /> <br /> The Demon Core Book gives an example of how to subvert Infrastructures: stealing Angelic Covers. Other examples are mentioned in passing throughout the supplements, but there is not enough mechanical guidance. Therefore, I have elaborated homebrew for this. Feel free to modify this system as needed for your Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Demons can apply certain Persistent Conditions to Infrastructures by investigating their inner workings until they reach a sufficiently comprehensive understanding of the underlying occult matrices. This is represented via the Clues System from the ChroD Core Book, with each main type of Infrastructure in any given city having at least one Clue associated with it. Therefore, Demons focus on gathering 5 categories of Clues: Defense, Elimination, Logistical, Concealment and Command &amp; Control.<br /> <br /> The aforementioned Persistent Conditions have a cost in Clue Elements for being implemented, and at least one Clue Element must come from the relevant category. The Ring will work most efficiently if the individual Demons have a well-rounded list of mundane and supernatural talents. Furthermore, this implementation requires that the Ring of Demons remove or neutralize the Linchpin and replace it with an equivalent version designed by them with the intention of editing the underlying occult matrices toward a different output.<br /> <br /> This frequently involves giving a specific input whose properties are in opposition to the Infrastructure's design. The process of securing components for the subversive Linchpin can be modeled as Social Maneuvering and Procurement between Agencies, the assemblage can be modeled as Crafting Equipment Actions, and the field missions for implementation of the Hijacking Conditions can be modeled as Chases backed up by Plans. Hijacking Conditions can be Resolved by deactivating and/or removing the key-components responsible for the subversion of the former Linchpin, which has different requirements, obstacles and side-effects that are unique to each Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> The Beats given by the Hijacking Conditions can be pooled with Beats from other sources to acquire unique Merits, which reflect the techno-gnostic insights received through extensive research and development focused on the underlying occult-physics. Any Genii who actively contribute to uncovering the Clue Elements necessary for establishing the Hijacking Conditions can receive Inspired Beats from them and thus replicate the Hijacked Merits for their Gadgets at the ST\u2019s discretion, with certain adjustments on a case by case basis. There may also be Advanced and even Epic versions of Hijacked Merits, but those certainly have proportionally extreme prerequisites, such as applying a Hijacking Condition to a Facility [DTD Core 242-243], forming a Pentagram-Cipher [DTD ST Guide 43], or even infiltrating the Apocalypse Vault.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Hijacking Conditions</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Waste Heat</b><br /> Gaining access to the Infrastructure's occult energy matrix, the Demon(s) infiltrate an intentional inefficiency in its processes; more energy is consumed than is necessary. Typically, the Infrastructure compensates for this elsewhere, so this Condition does not impact its overall function, but the &quot;lost&quot; energy is of enormous use to Demons. Its absence from the expected output means nobody will miss it when they stroll by and steal it. This Hijacking Condition costs 1 to 3 Clue Elements, and generates an equal amount of Aether every Chapter, analogously to Suborned Infrastructure Merit.<br /> <br /> Beat: The Demon's player declares that the waste heat has drawn the attention of a wandering Cryptid, who settles into the place like a cat crawling into a warm engine block.<br /> <br /> <b>Blind Spot</b><br /> The Infrastructure no longer sends or receives signals from other Infrastructure nodes; typically this is not a total &quot;blackout,&quot; but a false-tagged &quot;message received!&quot; that causes Infrastructure to believe it is communicating, but in truth their signals are lost to the void. Among other contextual benefits such as allowing the Ring to cripple that Infrastructure without the God-Machine becoming aware until it affects other nodes, this means that nothing the Demons do within that Infrastructure's area of influence risks Cover breach, unless it is witnessed by an agent of the God-Machine who can leave that area and then report. This Hijacking Condition costs 5 Clue Elements.<br /> <br /> Beat: This blind spot also means many auto-corrective signals are not sent or received. The Demon's player declares the Infrastructure has fallen into disrepair in some way, requiring manual tuning and maintenance that the God-Machine would have normally handled automatically.<br /> <br /> <b>Reprogramming</b><br /> The Infrastructure produces a different Angel than it was supposed to, and the Demons can modify traits of the Angel. This Hijacking Condition costs Clue Elements equal to [Angel's Rank X 2], and allows the Demons to edit the Ban, Bane, Numina, Influences, Manifestations, Virtue and Vice. However, the Demons cannot change the Angel's Rank, Incarnation, Incepts, or Mission, nor can they force the Angel to abandon its Mission, much less outright Fall.<br /> <br /> Beat: The Demon's player declares that a crucial part of the reprogramming goes haywire. This allows the ST to secretly make an edit of his own for the traits of the Angel, which must result in significant danger or destruction.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Hijacked Merits</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Engineering (\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> Prerequisites: Raw Materials Embed, Esoteric Adapter Process, Ephemeral Cover Exploit, Waste Heat Condition Tagged To The Underworld, Shadow Or Equivalent<br /> \ufeff<br /> The Demon is capable of synthesizing materials composed of ephemera via Raw Materials, and using the Esoteric Adapter to turn such ephemeral materials into devices that take advantage of the state of Twilight. This is modeled as a roll to Craft Equipment of the Mystic type, and the Demon can select any frequency of Twilight whose existence he is aware of, with the exception of the one inhabited by Angels.<br /> <br /> A common benefit of Exceptional Success for rolls is to allow the Mystic Equipment to count as a specific instance of effective Esoteric Armory with a Merit Rating of up to [Occult], as long as the Demon has fully Researched the relevant Ephemeral Being, Cryptid, Blue-Book Horror or equivalent entity. If the Supernatural Tolerance of this entity goes from 1 to 10, halve their Supernatural Tolerance (rounded up) to determine their effective Rank for the purposes of Esoteric Armory.<br /> <br /> As long as he is manifesting the Esoteric Adapter, the Demon can manually switch the Mystic Equipment between the Twilight and corporeal states as an Instant Action and without a roll. He can also engineer the Mystic Equipment in ways that allow it to switch its components into Twilight and back into corporeal state in various configurations, which in turn allows functions normally impossible for mundane Equipment. The Demon can make Stockpiles out of this Mystic Equipment, which is considered to have a Complexity equal to his [Occult].<br /> <br /> The Demon must be inside the appropriate otherworldly realm such as the Shadow or Underworld, or activate Raw Materials on an object tagged with the Open Condition for a Ghost, Spirit or equivalent entity whose type matches the Mystic Equipment. The entity can use its supernatural powers to generate the Open Condition for the object, and if both the Demon and the entity are inside an appropriate otherworldly realm, the roll for Crafting Mystic Equipment receives bonus dice equal to the entity\u2019s Rank, or its [Supernatural Tolerance/2 Rounded Up] if such a trait goes from 1 to 10.</div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",